Patch 3009: the tick-locked audio's output follows a sustained slow pace down (slight slow motion instead of gaps; AUDIO_LOCK_SLOW_MIN=0 turns it off).

Symptom (test8 bundles): a laptop that could not hold 30 fps ran the whole lockstep fight at about 20 ticks/s, on both PCs. A tick still mixes 6.25
blocks (patch 3005), so only 2/3 of the sound the device plays arrived; 3007 concealed the rest: 2680 concealed gaps (74 s) in 2.3 min on the joiner,
1446 on the host, with the level under the cushion and the rate control at its +3.12% cap. No buffer holds a sustained deficit.

Output only (blocks mixed, read index and notify events are exactly as in 3005; muted re-run blocks are never submitted, so they are never counted):
- the first block of each burst measures the arrival rate of the blocks (blocks per wall second against 187.5, times 1 + the feed-forward the
  resampler actually played for them, weighted by blocks) in 1 s buckets. Only the applied part counts: 3008 caps fb + ff at 8 %, so a test9
  time-sync stretch of 16.7 or 25 ms per tick (ff 0.5 / 0.75) is mostly a slow pace and engages it. It engages when the last 3 buckets were all under 95%: one hitch, even 300 ms, lowers at
  most two, so the cushion and the concealment keep the hitches as before;
- engaged, the playback rate (a factor on the 3007 resampler's step) follows the arrival rate of the last 3-4 s down at up to 0.2 per second, never
  under AUDIO_LOCK_SLOW_MIN % (default 60; 55 at least, so a block still fits in LK_OUTMAX; 0 or 100 = off), and not while the device holds more
  than the cushion. The level before the burst trims it by up to +-10% around 3/4 of the cushion (room for the surplus of a sudden recovery). Each
  burst's change is spread over its first 6 blocks, and one burst's ramps move at most 0.1 s worth (a stall does not snap the pitch);
- back: when the last 3 bursts arrive at 97% or more it returns to 1 at up to 1.5 per second and disengages once the level is near the cushion. The
  cushion feedback and the feed-forward are unchanged and work on top of it. With AUDIO_LOCK_SMOOTH=0 there is no resampler and no slow pace;
- the "[audio-lock]" line keeps every field and their order and appends: "slow pace: N times, X s, rate min R, floor F %, on|off": how often it
  engaged, how long it was engaged or under 1, the lowest playback rate (1.000 = never), the floor in effect;
- tests: libs/audio/tests/test_audio_lock_race.c part 5 drives the real output on a 200 ms fake device (cushion 90 ms, AUDIO_LOCK_DRC=8, as J-Stars
  sets them) in virtual time (s_lk_test_ms): steady 30 ticks/s and 76 ms / 150-300 ms hitches never engage and give the same counters as with it off;
  20 ticks/s (even, and with the 2 ms stretch) settles at 0.667 (0.707 with the stretch fed forward) with no concealed gap after 15 s (off: 900);
  20 then 30 ticks/s returns to 1 with nothing squeezed or dropped; an uneven ~20 ticks/s cuts the gaps after 15 s from 618 to 37; 12 ticks/s holds
  the 60% floor; 20 ticks/s made of 33.3 ms ticks plus a published 16.7 ms stretch, 23 ticks/s with 25 ms and 17 ticks/s with 25 ms engage with
  no gap after 15 s (off: 725-887); a 2 s stall while engaged moves the rate no more than one ordinary tick. audio_lock_measure.c adds "76 ms hitch every 12 s" and five slow-pace scenarios (two with big published stretches) (a line every 2 s, gaps from 15 s on).

